er and more expensive equipment. Lydrommet were kind enough to borrow me an ISA 828 preamp to do some testing. I\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"","width":0,"height":0},"classes":[]},{"id":79,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/10\/01\/equipment-standard-microphones-setup\/","url_meta":{"origin":493,"position":2},"title":"Equipment standard (microphones &#8211; setup)","date":"October 1, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"My main concern when it comes to microphones is that I want to feel they express the energy of my musical intentions. Until now, I\u2019ve let sound engineers use their own microphones and I\u2019ve used a split, a return bus or my own built-in microphones to get sound into my\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/11.png?fit=667%2C329&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":25,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/signal-flow\/","url_meta":{"origin":493,"position":3},"title":"Signal-flow","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"The audio from my EMFit based contact microphones goes into my sound card (Focusrite pro40), then to the DAW - Ableton Live, through desired effects and\/or to be stored on the hard drive, back to the sound card and out to a PA-system. Sound engineers usually treat my drums as\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"signal-flow","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/41.gif?fit=586%2C476&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":82,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/music-the-beginning\/","url_meta":{"origin":493,"position":4},"title":"Music &#8211; The Beginning","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"This is a recording from a solo concert I did early June 2011. The audio is just a stereo signal from my sound card, there are some audio drop-outs and I apologize for that. In general I feel the tendency of looping is to present and that it makes the\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"","width":0,"height":0},"classes":[]},{"id":362,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/10\/25\/project-description\/","url_meta":{"origin":493,"position":5},"title":"Project description","date":"October 25, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"Project description: Performance with realtime interaction between drums and electronics. Goal: To develop a setup with drums and electronics which shall be practical and easy to operate. Why I do this: Amongst guitarists and some what keyboard players, the integration of audio processing and the interaction between the instrument and\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"","width":0,"height":0},"classes":[]}],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/493"}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=493"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/493\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1900,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/493\/revisions\/1900"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1682"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=493"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/